  {
    "code": "SSC-EWI-0073",
    "description": "PENDING FUNCTIONAL EQUIVALENCE REVIEW FOR 'UpdateOfColumnName' NODE",
    "problem_description": "A cursor is declared FOR UPDATE OF with an explicit column list, which in SQL Server restricts positioned updates to those columns and influences the locks taken. Snowflake Scripting has read-only cursors with no positioned update and no column-level update declaration, so the clause was preserved for review but has no effect and the positioned updates it enabled cannot run.",
    "recommended_fix": "Drop the FOR UPDATE OF clause and convert the positioned updates into keyed updates or a single set-based statement. Include the target table's primary key in the cursor query, then inside the loop issue UPDATE target SET col = ... WHERE key = :loop_key, naming only the columns the clause listed so the intent stays visible. Better, eliminate the cursor: express the per-row computation as a query and apply it with one UPDATE joined to that query, or a MERGE, which both restricts the written columns naturally and avoids row-at-a-time execution. Do not try to reproduce the locking behaviour; use an explicit transaction around the statement if the read and write must be atomic."
