  {
    "code": "SSC-EWI-TS0041",
    "description": "XML TYPE METHOD exist IS NOT SUPPORTED IN SNOWFLAKE",
    "problem_description": "The source tests for the presence of an XML node with the .exist('xpath') method, which returns 1 when the path matches and 0 otherwise, typically in a WHERE clause or a CASE expression. Snowflake has no XML type methods, so the predicate cannot compile as converted.",
    "recommended_fix": "Replace the existence test with a NULL check on an XML navigation. Parse the document with PARSE_XML(col) and use XMLGET to reach the node, then test the result: XMLGET(PARSE_XML(col), 'Options') IS NOT NULL is the equivalent of .exist('/Options') = 1. For a nested path, chain XMLGET calls, and for a specific occurrence pass the instance number as XMLGET(node, 'Item', 0). Where .exist() tested for a node matching a value predicate, express it as a check over the flattened children instead: LATERAL FLATTEN the node set and apply the predicate in a semi-join or an EXISTS subquery. Keep the 1/0 result shape only if callers depend on it, by wrapping the NULL check in IFF."
