    "recommended_fix": "Rewrite the comparisons against what Snowflake can actually report. Replace XACT_STATE() = 0 with CURRENT_TRANSACTION() IS NULL and XACT_STATE() = 1 with CURRENT_TRANSACTION() IS NOT NULL. Delete the XACT_STATE() = -1 branch rather than leaving it unreachable, and move whatever it did, normally an unconditional ROLLBACK, into the EXCEPTION block so a failure always rolls back the transaction the procedure owns. Then re-read the handler as a whole: logic that distinguished recoverable from doomed transactions has no counterpart, so the handler should reduce to rollback, log and re-raise, and any retry that depended on a committable state must be reconsidered."
